mpounds are formed when atoms of different elements combine in any ratio. All the atoms of a given element have identical properties including identical \nmass.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f722ee0e063d9286d68"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f722ee0e063d9286d69", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfb1"], "topics": ["60e5671c499d1e49588f8809"], "concepts": ["60e5671a499d1e49588f87ef"], "question": {"text": "The pair, in which ions are isoelectronic with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Al</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> is"}, "options": [{"id": "706533", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Br</mi><mo>-</mo></msup></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Be</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f722ee0e063d9286d6a"}, {"id": "e8cfa7", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Cl</mi><mo>-</mo></msup></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Li</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f722ee0e063d9286d6b"}, {"id": "4785df", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup></math> and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f722ee0e063d9286d6c"}, {"id": "3d2648", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup></math> and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Mg</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f722ee0e063d9286d6d"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f722ee0e063d9286d6e", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfb1"], "topics": ["60e2fb5766f9ce3f243b4f49"], "concepts": ["60e2fb5666f9ce3f243b4f27"], "question": {"text": "According to Bohr's model of hydrogen atom, Which of the following statements is incorrect?"}, "options": [{"id": "0b4508", "text": "Radius of \\(3^{\\text {rd }}\\) orbit is nine times larger than that of \\(1^{\\text {st }}\\) orbit.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f722ee0e063d9286d6f"}, {"id": "55d23d", "text": "Radius of \\(8^{\\text {th }}\\) orbit is four times larger than that of \\(4^{\\text {th }}\\) orbit.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f722ee0e063d9286d70"}, {"id": "f2d7a4", "text": "Radius of \\(6^{\\text {th }}\\) orbit is three time larger than that of \\(4^{\\text {th }}\\) orbit.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f722ee0e063d9286d71"}, {"id": "44732a", "text": "Radius of \\(4^{\\text {th }}\\) orbit is four times larger than that of \\(2^{\\text {nd }}\\) orbit.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f722ee0e063d9286d72"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f722ee0e063d9286d73", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfb1"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b477c"], "concepts": ["60e2fb9d66f9ce3f243b52d5"], "question": {"text": "<p>It is observed that characteristic X-ray spectra of elements show regularity. When frequency to the power &#39;n&#39; i.e.&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></msup></math>&nbsp;of X-rays emitted is plotted against atomic number <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Z</mi></math>, the following graph is obtained.</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F4e1c29e0-4b73-4a2d-86ff-3bfaf28db468-9893742.PNG?alt=media\" style=\"width: 209px; height: 200px;\" /></p><p>The value of &#39;n&#39; is</p><p>&nbsp;</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "fdabc7", "text": "1", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f722ee0e063d9286d74"}, {"id": "ea033b", "text": "2", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f722ee0e063d9286d75"}, {"id": "910e7c", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f722ee0e063d9286d76"}, {"id": "b5b539", "text": "3", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f722ee0e063d9286d77"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f722ee0e063d9286d78", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfb1"], "topics": ["60e2fb2066f9ce3f243b4b78"], "concepts": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b42"], "question": {"text": "<p>What is the work function of the metal if the light of wavelength <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4000</mn><mover><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></mover></math> generates photoelectrons of velocity <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>5</mn></msup><mtext>&#8201;</mtext><msup><mi>ms</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> from it?</p><p>(Mass of electron <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>31</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math>, velocity of light <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>8</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>ms</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>, Planck&#39;s constant <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>.626</mo><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>34</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Js</mi></math>, Charge of electron <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>.626</mo><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>34</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Js</mi></math>)</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "c9bada", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.9</mo><mtext>&#8201;</mtext><mi>eV</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f722ee0e063d9286d79"}, {"id": "5cb71d", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>.0</mo><mtext>&#8201;</mtext><mi>eV</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f722ee0e063d9286d7a"}, {"id": "1ad7c6", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>.1</mo><mtext>&#8201;</mtext><mi>eV</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f722ee0e063d9286d7b"}, {"id": "b67b27", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>.1</mo><mtext>&#8201;</mtext><mi>eV</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f722ee0e063d9286d7c"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f722ee0e063d9286d7d", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfb1"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b478d"], "concepts": ["60e5678c499d1e49588f9268"], "question": {"text": "The number of orbitals associated with quantum numbers <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></math> is:"}, "options": [{"id": "f6bc38", "text": "<math><mn>11</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f722ee0e063d9286d7e"}, {"id": "e0998b", "text": "<math><mn>25</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f722ee0e063d9286d7f"}, {"id": "8ba422", "text": "<math><mn>50</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f722ee0e063d9286d80"}, {"id": "fe4537", "text": "<math><mn>15</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f722ee0e063d9286d81"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f722ee0e063d9286d82", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfb1"], "topic